## Context

Child of master ticket 0660. The current egress sweep drives install,
configure, resume and a query against an empty index. It does not drive a
populated build, so it cannot observe a path that exfiltrates library text only
while indexing. It also hand-lists fewer than the interface's seven verbs with
no coverage guard. This child owns path coverage, not the permitted-call ruling
(0661), relay detection (0663), or default-runtime setup (0664).

## Actions

- Provide a target-neutral way to populate a fixture with distinctive,
  non-secret library text and drive the target's real default build/update path.
- Trace startup, each offered public verb, background idle work and shutdown;
  explicitly classify paths that cannot carry R10 data rather than omitting
  them silently.
- Send a distinctive query and prove both query-bearing and library-text-bearing
  controls reach the detector.
- Generate or guard the lifecycle roster so a new verb/path cannot arrive
  untraced.

## Test

- [ ] A build-only text exfiltrator is red while a local build is green.
- [ ] A query-only exfiltrator is independently red.
- [ ] Empty or unbuilt premises report `not-run`, never PASS.
- [ ] Background and shutdown egress controls prove their observation windows.
- [ ] Removing a relevant path from the roster fails a fast guard.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Both R10 data classes are present and distinctive in the exercised run.
- [ ] Every relevant lifecycle path is traced or explicitly excluded with a
      checked reason.
- [ ] Focused fail-controls have been seen red before green.
- [ ] Real-target evidence is committed under `bench/results/`.
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` pass.
